# How to properly use Ant Design with TanStack Start #4052
created: 2025-05-08, last updated: 2026-08-09, [Read more](https://github.com/TanStack/router/discussions/4052)

You want `StyleProvider` + `extractStyle` on the server, injected into head before hydration.
In TanStack Start the cleanest hook is a root-route `head` function that calls `extractStyle(cache, true)` after render — without `true` you only get partial rules.
...
import { Outlet, createRootRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router';
...
Actually, the cleaner approach in TanStack Start is using the `Document` component in your root route:
```
// app/routes/__root.tsx
import { createRootRoute, HeadContent, Outlet, Scripts } from '@tanstack/react-router';
import { StyleProvider, createCache, extractStyle } from '@ant-design/cssinjs';
...
<StyleProvider cache={cache}>
<html>
<head>
<HeadContent />
{/* Ant Design styles will be injected here on server */}
...
<style dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: extractStyle(cache) }} />
...
}
export const Route = createRootRoute({
component: () => (
<Document>
<Outlet />
</Document>
),
});
...
1. **Cache mismatch**: You created `createCache()` in a layout route AND in `__root.tsx`.

